SUMMARY:Wissahickon Valley Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this diverse loop hike in the Wissahickon Valley featuring lot
 s of different trails and such.\nAfter meeting at the Acme in Flourtown\, 
 we will get on into part of Fort Washington State Park. We'll do all of th
 e trails on the south side of the creek\, then make our way onto some back
  streets and through ball fields south.\nHeading south\, we'll head into J
 ames A Cisco Park\, then cover a few more back streets to Morris Arboretum
 . There is a charge for this section\, I believe $10\, walk in fee which i
 s less than others. It should be a great time of year to see it\, and so w
 e'll spend more time there than we would have otherwise and try to do all 
 of the trails possible.\nAfter this visit\, we'll make our way into the Fa
 irmount Park sections view near connecting trails and meander through. Thi
 s will lead us across the Wissahickon\, and we'll then follow a circuitous
  route through the Andorra section\, through woods and meadows.\nAfter thi
 s\, we make our way back to Forbidden Drive\, and then follow the Green Ri
 bbon Trail back to the starting point. A portion of that is along a back r
 oad\, but there's plenty of grassy side to walk on that bit. The last stre
 tch will be directly along the Wissahickon in a pleasant section.\nIf need
 ed\, contact me at 908 343 8374
